{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["YHWH descended in the sight of all the people — one should say that the ״ויאמר ה׳״ at the beginning of the verse was through an angel. Therefore it says: ״יִרַד ה׳״ — and not the Holy One, blessed be He, Himself, since it is not written ״אֵרֵד״. As I explained regarding ״וה׳ המטיר על סדום״ and so forth — ״מאת ה׳ מן השמים״: the first is Gabriel and the second is the Holy One, blessed be He. And also in the Haggadot this is so."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The lemma reads 'in the sight of all the people' but the comment addresses the phrase 'YHWH descended'; the final clause וגם בהגדות ראשון שבפסוק is textually uncertain and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:07.991368526Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}